{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-10T14:43:04.434Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"e64a4bf384d39392d902ceda","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.322","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-gh1700"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"GH-1700: pm test --add returns only the changed linked test, like pm comments --add"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"GitHub issue 1700 (reported against 2026.11.10): every 'pm test <id> --add' echoes the item's whole linked-test list with provenance, plus a failure_categories block of nine zero counters. 'pm comments <id> --add' returns only the new entry, count/total_count/has_more, a mutation_receipt and an omission_receipt. The issue measures 485 B for a comment add on an item with 7 comments, 369 B for a test add with 2 linked tests and 3,335 B for a test add with 26 linked tests. Agents link 20-40 tests per item over a PR's life, so each add re-sends a list that grows linearly. Expected: one collection-mutation receipt shape across comments, files, docs and test. --add/--remove return only the changed entries, the counts and a mutation_receipt. failure_categories appears only for --run. The full list remains reachable through the omission_receipt restore flag. Observed in this session too: linking one test to pm-gh1699 echoed the full receipt. Duplicate check: searched 'test --add echoes linked tests receipt failure_categories' and 'collection mutation receipt files docs test add only changed entries'. pm-covpax (closed) compacted zero failure categories only on lean --run receipts, and pm-gh1630 (closed) bounded selective --run receipts. Neither covers the add/remove mutation receipt."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["agent-ux","gh:1700","linked-tests","receipts","token-efficiency"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-10T14:43:04.434Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-10T14:43:04.434Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":120},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"A test --add on an item with 26 linked tests returns a receipt whose size does not grow with the existing list, matching the comments --add shape; failure_categories is absent from add/remove receipts and unchanged on --run receipts; The omission_receipt names the flag or command that restores the full linked-test list, and executing it returns every linked test; files and docs --add are measured and follow the same shape when they share the code path; CLI, SDK and MCP receipts stay in parity"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-5t33or"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"low"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"pm test --add/--remove (and files/docs if they share the path) return only the changed entries plus count/total_count/has_more, a mutation_receipt and an omission_receipt; failure_categories appears only on --run."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-covpax","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-11-10T14:43:04.434Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-gh1630","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-11-10T14:43:04.434Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]}],"before_hash