{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-11T06:43:24.513Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"e6ba0f6f7044b066fe23d5ec","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-4yxzvd","claim:pm-gh1700","claim:pm-oglm0t","claim:pm-pwqiao","claim:pm-tuxw1i","lineage:pm-oglm0t","lineage:pm-f05lsg","lineage:pm-mpbb","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-4yxzvd+pm-gh1700+pm-oglm0t+pm-pwqiao+pm-tuxw1i","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-4yxzvd","claim:pm-gh1700","claim:pm-oglm0t","claim:pm-pwqiao","claim:pm-tuxw1i","lineage:pm-oglm0t","lineage:pm-f05lsg","lineage:pm-mpbb","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.322","source":"probe"}},"op":"note_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-11T06:43:24.513Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/notes","value":[{"created_at":"2026-11-11T06:43:24.513Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Implementation on branch fix/collection-mutation-receipts (2026-11-11).\n\nShape. The shared projectLinkedCollectionMutation in src/sdk/linked-artifacts.ts is exported from the SDK. Any test, files or docs write returns only the entries it added or rewrote. That covers add, addJson, addGlob, remove, removeIndex, migrate and a linked-test --update/--update-index edit. writtenLinkedEntries computes the written entries as a multiset diff by full stored value, so note revisions and migrations count as written. count is the number of returned entries and total_count the number stored, as in comments. mutation_receipt carries changed_count, removed_count and full_history_included. omission_receipt reuses AnnotationOmissionReceipt with the group name <collection>_history and the full_history selector (CLI --full-history, SDK fullHistory, MCP full). List reads are unchanged.\n\nRun-only fields. failure_categories is now optional and present only when the call ran tests. The implicit post-write validation covers the returned entries, and is omitted when none are returned. --validate-paths still checks every stored path. Internally the run path keeps the full list; only the projection is bounded.\n\nTransport wiring:\n- CLI: --full-history on files, docs and test (register-mutation.ts, register-operations.ts).\n- Flag contracts.\n- MCP completeness map ('--full-history' to 'full').\n- MCP tool-schema optional 'full'.\n- MCP actions map full to fullHistory through normalizeAnnotationTransportOptions.\n\nMeasured. pm test --add on an item with 26 linked tests now returns 900 B as JSON. The issue measured 3,335 B. The size is independent of the list: the spec compares a 3-test item with a 27-test one and they differ by at most one byte.\n\nSeam fixed. A measurement refusal's recovery rebuilds the invocation through buildBackgroundTestCommandArgs, which dropped --full-history. It now carries the flag, so a replayed write keeps the caller's receipt shape.\n\nCensus before tightening the contract. pm-vcs reads .tests only from list reads and run_results from runs. pm-web's client ignores the POST body and re-reads lists, and its contract test reads 'pm test <id>'. GitHub code search found no other consumer.\n\nSDK surface: acknowledged breaking (signature) with migration guidance in docs/SDK.md."}]}],"before_hash":"ad5c6b85a0bc2f4324cc5d7059871632cb510c0561953ad2743eb37e7bd65163","after_hash":"6260e6510187c6de6002f431c0cd31ddcf4c49c1db45a8fd4b00a0bbccbff831","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"a475a3f55aafff53eba67f786d996b16c7debd2a2a69aa949cdbad12ab2adf1c"}
