{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-11T08:42:40.108Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"e6ba0f6f7044b066fe23d5ec","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.322","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-11T08:42:40.108Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-11-11T08:42:40.107Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"PR 1705 review round 1 (Greptile P1), fixed. Doc and file writes could return an unchanged entry, because storage orders a collection by scope and then path while the draft sorts by path, and the receipt took the persisted entry at the draft's position. Written entries are now matched to the persisted collection by persisted value: persistedLinkedEntries and writtenLinkedEntries compare JSON round-tripped forms, so keys holding undefined do not count. The receipt returns them in stored order. A regression spec covers an existing global z.md plus a newly added project a.md."}]}],"before_hash":"4f074534b736d5e7a40b8b4e9a9327f37b72ae5d72bd107bae2e254af2741d6a","after_hash":"b436af17b1245d88352d1e0d516a739e556b4d7983554851fddebb397f122bec","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"9e67f599ed91f7215f8dafc088df2e99b155522853b1b441eece516f9accb328"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-11T09:27:35.115Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"e6ba0f6f7044b066fe23d5ec","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.322","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/1","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-11T09:27:35.115Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"PR 1705 review round 2 (Greptile P2 and Codex P2), fixed. Matching drafts to stored entries could still return an unsaved spelling, because storage canonicalizes more than undefined keys: linked-test paths go from backslashes to slashes, assertion arrays are sorted, and booleans are normalized. The receipt now diffs the persisted collection before the write (read under the lock) against the persisted collection after it, so no draft is ever reported. A spec adds a test with a backslash path through --add-json and checks that the receipt returns tests/a.mjs and that removing by that path matches. Also (Codex P2): an --add-glob that matches nothing used to fall into list mode and return the whole collection. Write intent now comes from the flags, so it returns a zero-change receipt; fullHistory still returns everything."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-11T09:27:35.115Z"}],"before_hash":"b436af17b1245d88352d1e0d516a739e556b4d7983554851fddebb397f122bec","after_hash":"933778dab104226b0df7a0c1ac67a07baa73b94b2c4e201c6b5f1a5a36bf18be","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"455d8ca2094e70467b3a5a667b4b16913345024fa58a272a8d52c98bf66225f1"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-11T10:01:18.810Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"e6ba0f6f7044b066fe23d5ec","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.322","source":"probe"}},"op":"update","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-11T10:01:18.810Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/contract_change","value":{"api":"runTest, runFiles, runDocs and pm test/files/docs writes","before":"A write returned the whole stored collection, count was the stored total, and failure_categories was always present","after":"A write returns only the entries it added or rewrote, with count (returned), total_count, mutation_receipt and omission_receipt; failure_categories appears only when tests ran","migrate":"Pass fullHistory (CLI --full-history, MCP full) to receive the whole collection after a write, read total_count for the stored total, and read failure_categories optionally"}}],"before_hash":"933778dab104226b0df7a0c1ac67a07baa73b94b2c4e201c6b5f1a5a36bf18be","after_hash":"38b3716ab21d378e02351a665ccd4f0404140f41ddae9b34a26a34f079e0a9df","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"45a7a43cb7bb1e32e73e975a6525d729302a28325999ca2034f74da9f8216516"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-11T11:04:27.659Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"e6ba0f6f7044b066fe23d5ec","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.322","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/2","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-11T11:04:27.659Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"PR 1705 review round 3 (Codex P2), fixed. mutation_receipt.removed_count for linked tests counted removals from the intermediate list. So an add and a remove of the same command in one call, on an item with no tests, reported removed_count 1 although nothing was ever stored. The receipt now counts stored tests with no same-identity entry left after the write (countRemovedStoredTests, using linkedTestsHaveSameIdentity on the persisted before and after lists). The legacy removed field keeps its meaning, and the zero-match removal refusal still relies on it. Spec: 'counts only stored tests as removed'. DeepScan's one new finding (NULL_POINTER, a spread of an optional retry array in linked-artifact-note-recovery.spec.ts) is fixed with a guarded retryArgsOf helper."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-11T11:04:27.659Z"}],"before_hash":"38b3716ab21d378e02351a665ccd4f0404140f41ddae9b34a26a34f079e0a9df","after_hash":"394c4a48ba1c5baa68d9ce9511da0255fd14e1c18acab85aa3785be338b5f8d0","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"0542350e1fc4194cffbbc079c00289686be072e09d4469240d1bc14b0426c45a"}
